## Findings
1. blocking — brief:59 Focus and expansion come apart after a successful answer to any non-first item when three or more are queued. In the prototype, `Inbox.tsx`'s reload sets `expandedId` to `petitiones[0]` once the answered id is gone, while `focusIndex` is clamped only by length. So after the Patron presses `j` to P-2 of P-1..P-3 and approves it, focus sits on P-3 and P-1 is expanded. From then on `1`/`2`/`3` silently do nothing (`resolveVerbAction` needs expanded === focused). P-1's ratio field also reads and writes P-3's stored reason (`reasonForPetition(reasons, focusedId)`), and success clears only P-1's entry, so the ratio typed for P-1 later pre-fills P-3. No existing row catches this: W-345-b6 answers item 2 of 2, where the clamp happens to re-align. The caller is the Patron working the queue. The result is a dead keyboard and a ratio field bound to a different petitio than the one shown. Replacement for brief:59: append "After a successful answer and reload, focus and expansion land together on `petitiones[reconcileFocusIndex(focusIndex, n)]`. The ratio field reads, writes and clears the expanded petitio's reason. A served b3 row answers the middle of three and then submits the new focused item with `1`." [severity: S1] [design: keeps] [class: spec×promise-unattainable-under-accepted-domain] — check: none: a served W-407-b3 row that answers the middle of three petitiones, then asserts `aria-selected` and the expansion are on the same item and that `1` posts that item's id with the ratio just typed
2. advisory — brief:53 The repository-relative evidence targets (`docs/`, `studio/`, `ci/`, `opera/`, `petitiones/`, `./`, `../`) resolve against the console origin. Its server serves only `/`, `/assets/` and `/api/` and answers anything else with a 404, so each anchor leaves the console for an error page and drops the typed ratio. A `#` target feeds the hash router (`parseRoute`), and an unknown hash falls back to Inbox. Brief:57 calls these "evidence links" with no such limit. Replacement for brief:53: append "Repository-relative and `#` anchors are rendered, not resolved: the console serves no repository file, so they open the server's 404 (or re-route the hash) until a file-serving opus exists; only `http(s)://` targets are promised to reach their target." [severity: S2] [class: spec×promise-unattainable-under-accepted-domain] — check: none: a served b2 row asserting the rendered href of each recognised form
3. advisory — brief:51 The two Colophons get "studio" from two different readers. `InboxResponse.studio` is the server's resolved absolute `studioDir`, while the Board's Colophon shows `/api/officina`'s manifest `studio` name (`Bisellium` / `Sample Studio`, the source `Colophon.tsx`'s doc comment names). The two screens will print different strings for the same officina, and the brief names neither reader nor the disagreement (D-070 C). The Input domain also has no row for this new served value. Replacement for brief:51: "`InboxResponse.studio?: string` is the server's resolved absolute `studioDir` (the officina path DIRECTION §4.5 names). It differs by design from the Board's manifest `studio` name, and the Inbox Colophon trusts only this field, falling back to `studio/` when it is absent." [severity: S2] [class: design×indirection-duplicates-source-of-truth] — check: none: a b5 assertion that the Colophon text equals the served `studio` value
4. advisory — brief:59 The Escape handler is a window listener. At 640/390, pressing Escape to close the W-415 sidebar overlay (Sidebar `onKeyDown`) bubbles to it and also collapses the expanded item. Replacement for brief:59: replace "Escape collapses without moving focus" with "Escape whose target is inside `.inbox` collapses without moving focus; an Escape handled by the shell overlay leaves the expansion unchanged". [severity: S4] [class: tests×ruled-case-uncovered] — check: none: a served 390 row that opens the overlay, presses Escape and asserts the expansion stays

## Verdict
The input boundary is sound (the `opened` front matter is a YAML-core string or other scalar, `instant()` rejects anything else as `—`, and the differ compares only state), but the prototype breaks focus–expansion agreement after answering a non-first item, which the brief neither prevents nor tests; that blocker keeps the design and goes to the build as a required fix.
VERDICT: FAIL
